@@ -15,3 +15,31 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## WebMCP browser tools
+
+The site exposes tools using the [WebMCP browser API](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp).
+In a supporting browser, agents can invoke `open_article_search` or
+`open_reading_list` from any page with the main header. The opened flyouts expose
+native HTML form tools:
+
+| Form tool | Parameters | Result |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `search_articles` | `query` | Matching article metadata and URLs; updates visible search results |
+| `manage_reading_list` | `action` (`view`, `add`, `remove`), `slug` (for add/remove) | Saved slugs and article metadata; updates the visible list and bookmarks |
+
+Form handlers read the browser-populated controls through `FormData` and return
+results using `SubmitEvent.respondWith`. Add and remove are idempotent, so retries
+cannot accidentally toggle a bookmark. The existing bookmark buttons still toggle.
+
+Article pages additionally expose `read_current_article` and
+`get_article_popularity`. The coffee, coastal, and plant articles respectively
+expose `get_coffee_brew`, `get_tide_levels`, and `get_plant_stats`. These utility
+tools use the app's base path, honor execution cancellation, and return HTTP
+status, redirect details, and response data. The demo's intentionally failing
+services remain unchanged; failures are returned as actionable tool results.
+
+Imperative tools use `use-webmcp-tool` for feature detection and registration
+cleanup when React islands unmount during Astro navigation. Browsers without
+WebMCP retain the standard forms and buttons. Native WebMCP availability depends
+on browser support and configuration in a secure context.
